{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Carroll&limit=10&title=Endless Forms Most Beautiful","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Endless forms most beautiful ","subTitle":"the new science of evo devo and the making of the animal kingdom "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Carroll, Sean B.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"Medical Subject Headings","#text":"Popular Work"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Popular works"},{"@authority":"Library of Congress Subject Headings","#text":"Popular works."}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York "}}],"dateIssued":[{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2005"},"c2005"],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Norton"},"edition":"1st ed."},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xi, 350 p., [16] p. of plates : ill. (some col.) ; 25 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Color content","#text":"polychrome"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"An introduction to evolutionary developmental biology demonstrates how the many forms of animals evolved and came into being, documenting how the Evo Devo branch of science proved that all animal organs and appendages, from arms and legs to wings and fins, were created from a small number of primitive genes."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Preface: Revolution #3 -- Introduction: Butterflies, zebras, and embryos -- pt. I: The making of animals -- Animal architect